1
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:09,540
大家好，我叫 Suhela，我将向大家展示我们对 Web API 结构及其数据模型的研究分析。
Hello everyone, my name is Suhela and I will be presenting to you our analysis on Web API structures and their data models.

2
00:00:09,998 --> 00:00:15,120
这是由我、法比奥·迪劳罗 以及 切萨雷·保塔索 教授共同完成的作品。
It's a work authored by me, Fabio DiLauro, and the professor Cesare Pautasso.

3
00:00:15,598 --> 00:00:20,080
我们都来自瑞士卢加诺 UZI大学的软件研究所。
We are all from the Software Institute at Uzi in Lugano, Switzerland.

4
00:00:22,286 --> 00:00:26,180
在这项工作中，我们对 Web API 进行了大规模的实证研究。
In this work, we perform the large-scale empirical study on web APIs.

5
00:00:26,606 --> 00:00:36,452
Web API 可能很小很简单，只提供少量的操作，但也可能非常庞大，
甚至无法在演示幻灯片上展示出来。
A web API can be small and simple, offering a small number of operations, as they
can be very large that they cannot even be visualized in a presentation slide.

6
00:00:37,134 --> 00:00:48,484
API 的规模是影响 API 管理、开发者使用体验、学习难度以及服务粒度的重要因素。
The size of an API is an important factor that impacts the API's governance, the experience of developers with the API,
also how much easy it is to learn it, and the service granularity.

7
00:00:48,878 --> 00:00:59,180
因此，在这项工作中，我们定义了一套指标，旨在从两个不同层面衡量 API：
结构层面和数据模型层面，数据模型描述了 API 结构中定义的操作所处理的资源。
So in that work, we defined a set of metrics in order to measure an API on two different levels,
on the level of its structure and its data model that describe the resources

8
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:03,524
因此，在这项工作中，我们定义了一套指标，旨在从两个不同层面衡量 API：
结构层面和数据模型层面，数据模型描述了 API 结构中定义的操作所处理的资源。
that are handled by the operations defined in the structure of the API.

9
00:01:04,590 --> 00:01:11,204
我们的方法是基于分析在 OpenAPI Specification 中编写的 Web API 描述。
Our approach is based on analyzing web APIs through their descriptions written in the Open API specification.

10
00:01:11,662 --> 00:01:18,080
为了构建数据集，我们前往 GitHub 搜索并下载了超过 100,000 个模型。
So for building our dataset, we went to GitHub and we searched and downloaded more than 100,000 models.

11
00:01:18,254 --> 00:01:31,588
我们对它们进行了去重，然后筛选出那些在其中一个端点处理 JSON 媒体类型数据的 API，
最终我们分析了超过 30,000 个模型。
We deduplicated them, then we filtered the ones describing APIs that are handling in one of their endpoints some data of JSON media
type, and at the end we ended up by analyzing more than 30,000 models.

12
00:01:33,166 --> 00:01:40,100
我们获取的这些大量的 OpenAPI Specification 已被解析和分析，旨在回答一系列问题。
This large number of OpenAPI specifications we cut have been parsed and analyzed in order to answer a set of questions.

13
00:01:40,846 --> 00:01:44,292
首先，我们分析的 API 到底有多大？
First, how big are actually the APIs we're analyzing?

14
00:01:44,718 --> 00:01:52,132
在我们的研究中，API 的规模被定义为其结构的规模和数据模型的规模。
The size of the API, in our case, is defined as both the size of its structure and the size of its data model.

15
00:01:52,622 --> 00:01:54,340
这引出了第二个问题。
Which leads us to a second question.

16
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:59,812
API 结构的规模与其数据模型之间是否存在任何关系？
Is there any relationship between the size of the API structures and their data models?

17
00:02:00,174 --> 00:02:08,900
换句话说，如果一个 API 非常庞大且提供很多操作，是否意味着它的数据模型也同样庞大？
Or in other words, if an API is so big and it offers a lot of operations,
does it mean necessarily that its data model is also that large?

18
00:02:10,382 --> 00:02:14,564
另一个问题主要与 API 的数据模型有关。
Another question is mainly related to the data models of the APIs.

19
00:02:15,150 --> 00:02:19,044
在同一个 API 内部，数据模式（Schema）是否存在重用？
Is there any reuse of data schemas within the same API?

20
00:02:19,758 --> 00:02:35,012
最后，为了避免过度概括并观察前几个问题的答案如何受 API 风格的影响，
我们将数据集划分为具有相同结构风格的各个子集。
And finally, to avoid overgeneralization and see how the answers of the previous questions are affected by the API style,
we segmented our dataset focused on each subset of APIs sharing the same structural style.

21
00:02:35,598 --> 00:02:40,100
然后我们对数据集的每个片段进行了相同的分析。
We then performed the same analysis on each of the segments of the dataset.

22
00:02:40,974 --> 00:02:47,492
当我们谈论 API 的规模时，根据我们选择的衡量指标，可能会得到很多不同的答案。
When we talk about the size of an API, we can receive a lot of answers depending on the metric we chose to measure it.

23
00:02:47,982 --> 00:02:50,052
让我们从结构的规模开始。
Let's start by the size of the structures.

24
00:02:51,118 --> 00:02:57,956
Web API 的 OpenAPI 描述包含了提取并绘制其树状结构所需的所有细节。
Open API descriptions of web APIs contain all the needed details to extract and draw their tree structure.

25
00:02:58,574 --> 00:03:02,500
基于这种结构表示，我们定义了我们的规模指标。
Based on this structure representation, we defined our size metrics.

26
00:03:03,022 --> 00:03:10,052
第一个指标是路径数量，即 API 原始描述中列出的路径数量。
The first one is the number of paths, which are simply the number of paths listed in the original description of the API.

27
00:03:10,478 --> 00:03:12,452
第二个指标是操作数量。
The second one is the operations.

28
00:03:12,782 --> 00:03:16,164
这也可以从 OpenAPI 描述的细节中提取出来。
This can be also extracted from the OpenAPI descriptions details.

29
00:03:17,582 --> 00:03:24,196
从这两个指标中，我们可以计算出一个新指标，即每个 API 的每条路径的操作数量。
From these two metrics, we can compute a new metric which is the number of operations per path for each API.

30
00:03:25,230 --> 00:03:27,108
我们的第四个指标是宽度。
Our fourth metric is the breadth.

31
00:03:27,406 --> 00:03:31,076
在示例中的 API 情况下，宽度等于 1。
In the case of the API in the example, the breadth is equal to 1.

32
00:03:31,502 --> 00:03:42,240
它被定义为直接连接到根节点的节点数量，这意味着在这种情况下，
该 Web API 的所有路径都以 user 段开头。
It is defined as the number of nodes that are directly connected to the boot, which
means also in that case that all the paths of this API start by the segment user.

33
00:03:42,766 --> 00:03:46,160
同时我们可以看到，这个 Web API 的多样性更高。
While we can see that in this API there is more diversity.

34
00:03:46,606 --> 00:03:48,612
这个 Web API 的宽度等于 5。
The breadth of this API is equal to 5.

35
00:03:49,870 --> 00:03:55,300
另一个指标是深度，也就是树结构的最高深度。
Another metric is the depth, which is simply the maximum depth of the tree structure.

36
00:03:56,046 --> 00:04:00,644
最后一点是 Web API 中使用的 HTTP 方法。
And then last but not least, the HTTP methods used in the API.

37
00:04:00,846 --> 00:04:05,252
在这种情况下，我们使用了五种不同的 HTTP 方法。
In that case, we have usage of five different HTTP methods.

38
00:04:06,030 --> 00:04:20,004
基于这些指标，我们发现大多数 Web API 及其研究包含少于 50 条路径，
少数几个包含超过 100 条路径，甚至有一个 Web API 的路径达到了 271 条。
Based on these metrics, we found that the majority of the APIs and their study have less than 50 paths,
and some few ones have more than 100 paths, going even up to 271 paths in the case of one API.

39
00:04:20,526 --> 00:04:28,036
而同一个 Web API 在所有操作中实际上只使用了一种方法，其宽度等于 1。
And that same API uses actually only one method in all its operations, and its breadth is equal to 1.

40
00:04:28,814 --> 00:04:36,036
在某些 Web API 中，宽度达到了 80，而最深的树拥有多达 80 个嵌套节点。
The breadth goes up to 80 in the case of some APIs, while the deepest tree have up to 80 nested nodes.

41
00:04:36,718 --> 00:04:49,508
一些 Web API 的端点使用 8 种不同的操作，因此使用 8 种不同的 HTTP 方法，
平均每个 Web API 使用超过两种 HTTP 方法。
Some APIs have endpoints using 8 different operations, and so using 8 different HTTP methods,
with an average of more than two HTTP methods used per API.

42
00:04:50,542 --> 00:04:54,852
Web API 的操作处理不同数据模式的资源。
The operations of Web APIs handle resources of different data schemas.

43
00:04:55,152 --> 00:05:09,764
在我们的工作中，我们从 API 描述中提取这些数据模型，追踪概念与操作之间的关系，
其中数据模式被用于描述 OpenAPI 模型中的请求和响应。
In our work, we extract these data models from the API's descriptions, keeping track of the relationships between the concepts and the
operations where the data schemas are used to describe a request for a response in the OpenAPI models.

44
00:05:10,478 --> 00:05:26,596
这里的每个类代表一个资源数据模式，它们之间的组合关系由这些组合符号表示，
箭头将它们连接到操作上，它们可以向我们展示每个数据模式实际上被使用在哪里。
Each class here represents a resource data schema, and the composition relations between them are depicted by these composition
notations, and the arrows are connecting them to the operations and they can show us where each data schema is actually used.

45
00:05:27,118 --> 00:05:33,316
因此，基于这种查看 Web API 数据模型的方式，我们使用以下指标来定义其规模。
So based in this way of seeing the API's data models, we define its size using the following metrics.

46
00:05:34,254 --> 00:05:42,500
首先，我们简单地计算 API 模型中定义的模式总数，同时我们也计算实际使用的模式数量。
First, we simply count the total number of schemas defined in the API
model and we also count the number of schemas that are actually used.

47
00:05:42,798 --> 00:05:48,992
从这些模型中，我使用的模式是指任何可以从 API 的操作之一到达的模式。
From these models, I used schema is any schema that is reachable from one of the operations of the API.

48
00:05:49,198 --> 00:05:55,908
从这两个指标中，我们还可以计算每个模式在 Web API 数据模型中的使用率。
And from these two metrics we can also compute the usage rate of each schema in a data model of an API.

49
00:05:56,112 --> 00:06:04,356
我们发现大多数 Web API 的数据模型由至少三个定义的模式组成，
而且其中大多数有两个模式被使用。
We found that most of the API's data models are composed of at least three defined schemas,
and also most of them have two schemas that are used.

50
00:06:05,006 --> 00:06:08,740
然而，在大多数情况下，所有定义的模式实际上都被使用了。
However, in most of them, all of the defined schemas are actually used.

51
00:06:09,294 --> 00:06:23,300
最大的数据模型由 580 个定义的模式组成，其中甚至不到一半被使用；
而使用率达到 100% 的最大数据模型由 386 个模式组成。
The largest data model is composed of 580 defined schemas, where not even half of them are used,
and the largest data model with a usage rate of 100% is composed of 386 schemas.

52
00:06:23,662 --> 00:06:34,532
现在我们使用定义的指标测量了 Web API 结构及其数据模型的规模，
我们还可以通过查看这些指标数值之间的相关性来回答第二个问题。
Now that we measure the sizes of the API structures and their data models using the defined metrics,
we can also answer the second question by looking at the correlations between the values of these metrics.

53
00:06:35,072 --> 00:06:48,388
通过这样做，我们发现最高的相关性出现在 API 模型中定义的模式数量与结构中定义的端点数量
之间，这可以从图表中的数据点分布中看出。
Doing so, we found that the highest correlations are spotted between the number of defined schemas in the API model and the number of
endpoints defined in its structure, which can be perceived from the data points distribution in the plot.

54
00:06:49,230 --> 00:06:56,292
下一个最高相关性是实际使用的模式数量（而非仅
在模型中定义的数量）与路径数量之间的相关性。
The next highest correlation is between the number of schemas that are
actually used, not only defined in the model, and the number of paths.

55
00:06:56,814 --> 00:07:03,716
这可以简单地解释为，实际上在大多数 Web API 中，大多数定义的模式都被使用了。
This can be simply explained by the fact that actually in most of the APIs, most of the defined schemas are used.

56
00:07:04,366 --> 00:07:13,316
第三高的相关性是定义的或使用的模式数量与 Web API 结构的宽度之间的相关性。
The third highest correlation is between the number of Unix schemas defined or used and the breadth of an API structure.

57
00:07:13,792 --> 00:07:23,556
这个结果意味着，在某些 Web API 的情况下，宽度实际上
可以作为一个反映 Web API 处理的资源类型多样性的指标。
This result means that in the case of some APIs, the breadth can be actually
a metric that reflects the diversity of resources type handled by the API.

58
00:07:23,918 --> 00:07:33,732
为了回答关于同一 Web API 内模式重用的第三个问题，
我们定义了新的指标来计算数据模型中重用的模式数量。
To answer the third question regarding the reuse of schemas within the same API,
we defined new metrics that computes the number of reused schemas in a data model.

59
00:07:33,998 --> 00:07:41,028
从我们的展示来看，这些模式可以通过找到那些与操作连接的箭头多于一个的模式来识别。
From our presentation, these schemas can be spotted by finding the ones having more than an arrow connecting them to an operation.

60
00:07:41,902 --> 00:07:48,484
我们还定义了重用率指标，它反映了在所有使用的模式中重用模式的数量。
And we also defined the reuse rate metric, which reflects the number of reused schemas among the total used ones.

61
00:07:49,422 --> 00:07:56,676
我们发现的一个有趣结果是，在大多数 Web API 中，至少有一个模式被重用。
One of the interesting results we found is that in most of the APIs, there is at least one schema that is reused.

62
00:07:57,230 --> 00:08:04,932
甚至在某些案例中，重复使用的模式数量超过150个，而且在某些情况下，重用率甚至达到了100%。
Even in a case, the number of reused schemas was more than 150, and the reuse rate in some cases reaches 100%.

63
00:08:05,966 --> 00:08:16,324
我们也能清楚地看到，重用概率与API的数据模型大小
高度相关，且在数据模型更大时，重用率也会增加。
We can also clearly see that the chance of reuse is highly correlated with
the API's data model sizes and increases in the case of larger data models.

64
00:08:17,166 --> 00:08:23,588
虽然我们可以看到，API结构的大小与数据模型的重用之间存在微弱的相关性。
While we can see a weak correlation between the size of the API structures and the data models reuse.

65
00:08:23,982 --> 00:08:33,188
所以为了看看之前的结论在缩小数据集范围时会发生什么变化，
我们根据API的结构风格对数据进行了细分。
So to see how the previous results would change, if we focus on a smaller subset of the dataset,
we segmented the data by structural styles of the APIs.

66
00:08:33,549 --> 00:08:41,092
我们区分了五种风格，其中read-only是仅包含get方法的API，它是最大的细分部分。
We distinguish five styles, the read-only, which are the APIs that have only get methods, and it is the largest segment.

67
00:08:41,582 --> 00:08:56,420
接着是RPC风格，即允许使用POST方法进行写入的API；还有读写型，典型的CRUD，
以及我们将任何其他类型的组合方法API归入一个叫REST的类别。
Then we have the RPC style, which are APIs allowing to write using POST method, the read and writes, the typical CRUD,
and we put in a category we called REST any other API using any other type of methods combinations.

68
00:08:57,454 --> 00:09:09,540
我们发现，read-only和RPC风格的API更有可能是小型API，
而CRUD和REST是结构上更大API中最常见的风格。
So we found that the APIs of RED-only and RPC styles are more likely to be small,
while the CRUD and REST are most common styles of structurally larger APIs.

69
00:09:10,190 --> 00:09:27,876
关于数据模型的大小，我们发现拥有最大数据模型的API是我们的REST风格，
而模式的使用情况在所有定义的风格中几乎相似，比例也差不多。
Regarding the data model sizes, we found that the APIs that have a more largest data model are the ones of our REST style,
while the usage of schemas is almost similar, of similar proportions for all the styles we defined.

70
00:09:29,006 --> 00:09:34,148
最后，为了总结，我想回顾一下本次演讲的主要观点。
And finally, to conclude, I would like to recapitulate the main points of this presentation.

71
00:09:34,670 --> 00:09:37,184
首先，我向大家介绍了这项工作的背景。
First, I put you in the context of the work.

72
00:09:37,390 --> 00:09:50,980
然后我向大家展示了我们分析的数据量，以此来获取关于API大小、
API结构与数据模型大小之间的相关性、API数据模型中使用了多少模式，以及最后，
then I showed you the amount of data we analyzed to get answers about the API sizes,
the correlations between the API structures and the data model sizes, about how much schemas are used in the API's data models,

73
00:09:50,980 --> 00:09:53,260
然后我向大家展示了我们分析的数据量，以此来获取关于API大小、
API结构与数据模型大小之间的相关性、API数据模型中使用了多少模式，以及最后，
and finally, if the size of each of the structures and the data models has something to do with the structural style of the API.

74
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:59,108
每个结构和数据模型的大小是否与API的结构风格有关。
and finally, if the size of each of the structures and the data models has something to do with the structural style of the API.

75
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:05,744
感谢您的观看，如果您有任何问题，欢迎随时联系我们。
And thank you for watching and If you have any questions, feel free to reach us.

